/Users/maxghenis/PolicyEngine/populace/packages/populace-build/src/populace/build/us/take_up_contract.json:27:      "notes": "SNAP take-up is seeded by the snap_take_up source stage (reported-receipt-anchored on raw ASEC SPM_SNAPSUB, national FNS rate fill, gated by snap_take_up_signal), then recalibrated per state by the snap_state_take_up stage to FNS average-monthly household caseloads among eligible non-anchored units (anchored count-calibration, medicaid_take_up pattern, gated by snap_state_take_up) — CPS receipt underreporting is state-dependent, so the national fill alone starves the worst-underreporting states of taker households (populace#372). The sourced national rate remains the prior, so this entry stays out_of_scope for this module's Bernoulli seeding rather than count_calibrated (that treatment forbids a sourced rate); out_of_scope means out of scope for this module's seeding, not unseeded."
/Users/maxghenis/PolicyEngine/populace/packages/populace-build/src/populace/build/us/take_up_contract.json:45:      "notes": "tanf formula multiplies summed state TANF benefits by takes_up_tanf_if_eligible, exactly like SNAP. No reported-TANF-receipt column (ASEC PAW_VAL) is threaded through the populace base spine, so the #294 reported-receipt anchor does not apply without base-pool changes (out of scope); TANF therefore uses calibrated Bernoulli at the administrative rate. us-data pinned 0.22 but mislabeled the vintage as 2018; the value is corroborated at 21.9% for 2022 and used with the correct vintage."
