/Users/maxghenis/PolicyEngine/populace/packages/populace-build/src/populace/build/us/state_program_reforms.json:45:   "description": "Gap analysis (2026-07 audit): +38.7% vs TY2023 splits into ~+5% benchmark vintage (max credit $1,117 TY2023 -> $1,154 TY2024; claims grew ~2%/yr) and ~+30% take-up \u2014 the sim pays every eligible unit and implies ~513k claiming units at the flat max vs FTB's 398,059 actual TY2023 returns (~78% implied take-up; CalEITC take-up measured at 54% among CalFresh-enrolled, California Policy Lab/JPubE 2023). A flat per-return credit passes the take-up gap straight to the total. Gap analysis (2026-07 audit): +38.7% vs TY2023 = ~6pp benchmark vintage (max $1,117 -> $1,154, phase-out start $25,775 -> $26,626: +6.2% measured on the same data) + ~30pp take-up. The model pays every eligible unit: 546-559k eligible units in the data vs FTB's 398,059 actual returns (claim/eligible 0.71-0.73, matching published take-up: CalEITC 54% among SNAP-enrolled per CPL/JPubE 2023). Per-unit amounts align ($1,025 sim vs $1,037 actual) \u2014 the gap is purely excess unit count; demographics ruled out (weighted CA under-6 is 6.2% BELOW ACS 2024). A flat per-return credit passes the take-up gap straight to the total."
